  "worked_solution": "The temperature decreases by $\\frac{3}{8}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each minute.\n\nSince the temperature decreases, the change each minute is $-\\frac{3}{8}.$\n\nThe change occurs for $\\frac{10}{3}$ minutes, so the total change is\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{3}\\times (-\\frac{3}{8}).\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{3}\\times (-\\frac{3}{8})=-\\frac{10\\times 3}{3\\times 8}=-\\frac{10}{8}=-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature is $-\\frac{5}{4}{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$",
